    {
      "id": 97,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        740,
        610
      ],
      "size": [
        300,
        160
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: KSampler settings",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "You can test and find the best setting by yourself. The following table is for reference.\n\n| Model            | Steps | CFG |\n|---------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Offical             | 50               | 4.0               \n| fp8_e4m3fn             | 20                | 2.5               |\n| fp8_e4m3fn + 4steps LoRA    | 4               | 1.0               |\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 116,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -612.9902954101562,
        593.4228515625
      ],
      "size": [
        290,
        140
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "The example images can be is [man.png](https://huggingface.co/datasets/nunchaku-tech/test-data/resolve/main/inputs/man.png), [puppy.png](https://huggingface.co/datasets/nunchaku-tech/test-data/resolve/main/inputs/puppy.png) and [sofa.png](https://huggingface.co/datasets/nunchaku-tech/test-data/resolve/main/inputs/sofa.png)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 113,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        730,
        1073.740234375
      ],
      "size": [
        330,
        90
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 4,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: About image size",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "You can use the latent from the **EmptySD3LatentImage** to replace **VAE Encode**, so you can customize the image size."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 96,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -240.9442596435547,
        1055.2066650390625
      ],
      "size": [
        290,
        140
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "This node is to avoid bad output results caused by excessively large input image sizes. Because when we input one image, we use the size of that input image.\n\nThe **TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus** will scale your input to 1024×104 pixels. We use the size of your first input image. This node is to avoid having an input image size that is too large (such as 3000×3000 pixels), which could bring bad results."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
